prompts.prompt:
Use case: precise-object-edit.
Image 1 is the EDIT TARGET: the CORVETTE five-view sheet. Image 2 is the authoritative original CORVETTE top plan. Make a targeted correction to the THREE RIGHT-HAND VIEWS and the rest pose of the two rear guns in TOP. Preserve the two left-hand plan drawings, their armor, fully detailed BOTTOM, silhouette, colors, original Corvette identity, all labels and white background. This is not a redesign.

The current right-hand FRONT and BACK are elevated bird's-eye shapes compressed vertically. Replace them with true LEVEL ORTHOGRAPHIC ELEVATIONS. The current SIDE borrowed the Cruiser hull and omitted one gun station; replace it with the side profile of the actual Corvette in TOP.

FIRST: in TOP, retain all four turret housings at their exact locations. Change only the two lower/rear pairs of barrels so they point straight UP, parallel to the upper guns, all toward the bow. Four twin-barrel mounts in two left/right pairs. Do not alter any hull panels.

FRONT: camera on the nose axis at exactly zero elevation, no perspective. The fore-aft direction points out of the paper; ALL NOSE-TO-TAIL LENGTH DISAPPEARS. Draw a broad, shallow armored cross-section, about four times wider than it is tall. A small blunt central nose END overlaps the hull and part of the bridge; its face is a compact trapezoid, never a long downward-pointing spine. The compact bridge is a small raised block behind it. Shoulder armor is seen edge-on as thick horizontal/sloped ledges, without broad roof planes or a recognizable squashed top-view ship. Two forward turret faces are above the shoulder ledges, with FOUR SMALL ROUND DARK MUZZLE HOLES pointed toward the viewer. The rear turret pair is hidden directly behind the forward pair at their matching lateral stations. Show convincing ventral armor below the shoulder ledges. No front-facing giant vents in the center nose, no empty aft turret sockets, no rear engine faces, no long fuselage sticking down toward the FRONT label.

BACK: same width and height as FRONT, camera exactly level looking forward along the thrust axis. Exactly TWO large circular cyan exhaust apertures, side by side at the SAME height, with layered dark/gunmetal concentric rims and silver upper cowls. The centerline tail is a short solid plated block between them. The wide forward shoulders are visible EDGE-ON beyond the engines as low horizontal armored ledges, not top-view wings. Low bridge partly visible above center. For gun stations seen from behind, draw SOLID REAR TURRET HOUSINGS; all forward-facing barrels and muzzle holes are occluded. Do not show bright circular gun muzzles facing backward or upright twin barrel lengths. No long tapered nose rising behind the engines. No perspective.

SIDE: create a new exact flat port-side elevation of THIS CORVETTE. Nose LEFT, stern RIGHT. Camera has ZERO ELEVATION and ZERO YAW, absolutely no roof surfaces visible. Use the top plan to place components, with nose 0% and nozzle 100% of length:
- compact reinforced bow 0–18%;
- tiny command bridge centered about 21%;
- first near-side turret center about 25%;
- second near-side turret center about 40%;
- the wide forward armored shoulder extends from about 18% to 49%;
- rear body becomes visibly narrower in top view, but in this SIDE it is a long low plated service hull from 49% to 80%;
- aft engine housing runs 74–100%, as one horizontal cylinder terminating in an edge-on vertical nozzle rim at the right.
Show BOTH near-side gun housings as two distinct low roofline silhouettes, with BOTH pairs of barrels pointing LEFT. The far-side pair is hidden behind its near-side counterparts. No extra third mount. The side bridge must not grow into a cruiser tower. Keep a compact thick armored belly with service panels, dark cooling grilles and brass connectors. At the stern, the two symmetric engines overlap in side projection. Show one near cylinder silhouette, not two stacked engines or an exhaust circle aimed at the side camera. Do not show a large shoulder roof, top deck, far wing or tilted rear cap. No hangar or tiny docked ship.

Consistent SCALE: use the existing TOP as ruler. SIDE length equals TOP length. FRONT and BACK width equals TOP beam. FRONT and BACK height equals SIDE height. Center the corrected views in their existing right column without touching labels.

Preserve exactly five drawings and the exact six labels "CORVETTE", "TOP", "BOTTOM", "FRONT", "BACK", "SIDE". Preserve the original pale titanium, charcoal gunmetal, brass and cyan details. Keep BOTTOM fully textured and free of dorsal guns/bridge. Clean precise technical illustration, no shadow, no scene, no inset, no additional text.
